      "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nThe `sequence_modes` property currently asserts the NumPy array itself. Multiple items raise an ambiguous-truth-value error, and a valid single mode 0 is rejected. Check for `None` instead, preserving the existing unimodal rejection while returning valid empty and nonempty mode arrays.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted draft. Human author review and NVIDIA GPU/CI validation are pending.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none; this is a narrowly scoped reproduced bug fix.\n\n## Validation\n\nActual multimodal builder/write/read regressions failed for empty modes, one zero, and multiple modes. The six-case matrix includes a nonzero singleton and the existing unimodal rejection. An empty corpus uses the supported file reader instead of an unrelated zero-length mmap.\n\n- Focused CPU validation: **6 passed** using actual production imports and generated fixtures; no production modules or functions are replaced by stubs.\n- Command: `/opt/cpu-review/bin/python -m pytest --confcutdir=tests/unit_tests/data tests/unit_tests/data/test_sequence_modes.py -q`.\n- CPU environment: Linux container, Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.8 CPU, real Triton package for imports. `--confcutdir` excludes the parent suite's unrelated GPU/data fixtures; this is not the canonical NVIDIA development image or full distributed test run.\n- Repository `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` completed successfully: Black, isort, Pylint and Ruff blocking checks passed.\n- The formatter's informational mypy step reports 27 indexed_dataset diagnostics. The same 27 diagnostic messages are present in baseline; its configured blocking checks pass.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [x] I have run the repository autoformatter\n\nNo GPU kernel is added or modified.\n",
